TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_5745_6741';
<p>5745_6741</p> <p>A phenotypically <i>wildtype</i> prospective couple seeks genetic counseling. The man has a <strong>balanced translocation</strong>, between chromosomes 4 and 5.This means that a segment of chromosome 4 has been exchanged with a segment of chromosome 5 without any gain or loss of genetic material. While balanced translocations typically do not affect the individual's phenotype, they can result in different types of gametes during reproduction.</p><p><ul><li><strong>Chromosome Pair:</strong> 4, 5</li><li><strong>Segregation Type:</strong> adjacent-2</li></ul></p><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white;"><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="104.0"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="320.0"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: small"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightsalmon" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">4</td><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="99.19999999999999"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="303.2"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: small"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightskyblue" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">5</td><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="104.0"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="160.0"></colgroup><colgroup width="151.6"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightsalmon" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">4</td><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black; border-right: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black; border-left: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="99.19999999999999"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="151.6"></colgroup><colgroup width="160.0"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightskyblue" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">5</td><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black; border-right: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black; border-left: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><p>all four of the chromosomes present in a somatic cell are shown above</p><p></p><p>Below are all the possible gametes produced by the man with the translocation.</p> <p>Among the six choices below, only two (2) gametes or two (2) sets of chromosomes are formed by <strong>adjacent-2</strong> segregation.</p> <p>Your task is to <strong>select the two (2) gametes produced by adjacent-2</strong> segregation.</p><p>CHECK TWO BOXES below!</p>
PROMPT_5745_6741
